From d933c660a042bd291511cba53b9cfb444d49fbaa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "chak-kei.lam" <chak-kei.lam@mediatek.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Jan 2026 16:35:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: release PPE tables on remove

The controller-wide PPE flow table and each PPE's L2 flow table remain
allocated when the Ethernet platform driver is removed.

Patch 758 already initializes the shared flow table once and keeps the
probe-error cleanup separate from per-PPE cleanup. Preserve that ordering
on the successful remove path: unregister the netdevs first, then destroy
the shared flow table and the per-PPE tables exactly once.

Link: https://github.com/mediatek/mtk-openwrt-feeds/blob/f7eec2ff2e4fc8ded3439d7805c0aaa030ef9e07/25.12/files/target/linux/mediatek/patches-6.12/999-ppe-33-net-ethernet-mtk_eth_soc-fix-mtk_eth_offload_init-memory-leak.patch
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -6062,6 +6062,11 @@ static void mtk_remove(struct platform_d
 
 	mtk_napi_del(eth);
 	mtk_cleanup(eth);
+	if (eth->soc->offload_version) {
+		rhashtable_destroy(&eth->flow_table);
+		mtk_ppe_deinit(eth);
+	}
+
 	free_netdev(eth->dummy_dev);
 	mtk_mdio_cleanup(eth);
 }
